These codes depend on two garden-variety library pacakages available on Linux,
MacOSX, and other POSIX-like platforms: (a) glib2-dev (b) libxml2.
These can be installed routinely using yum, fink etc (favourite package manager)
on your platform.

A few comments on porting experiences so far....

___________________________________________________________________

Intel Linux (32 bit), e.g. Redhat, Fedora etc

Reasonably heavily tested on this platform. Defaults should build.

___________________________________________________________________

Mac OSX

These code build fine (with a little effort) under Mac OSX.  Most
linux-like extra things can be pulled down using the fink package manager
http://fink.sourceforge.net/

Install these via % fink install .....

libxml2
glib2-dev
pkgconfig



Notes: Apple's gcc don't yet support thread-local storage under
Darwin, so some of the libraries aren't thread-safe (look for
__APPLE__ type #ifdefs in the code). DeliveryMassager doesn't use
threads anyway, so this is not an issue. But if the libraries end up
being called in a multi-threaded environment, this must be patched up
on OSX.

For ATLAS substitutes on intel macs, ATLAS also comes as part of the
development environment for those who may have trouble building ATLAS
on newer macs. Provided you have the development environment and
"Accelerate" framework in place, the build will detect "Darwin" as
part of your $CSIRO_OSTYPE and try to link against these libraries.
To check if you have this, see if you have the headers cblas.h,
clapack.h in /System/Library/Frameworks/vecLib.framework/Headers/
